Lazy loading is a performance optimization technique where resources are loaded only when they are needed,
instead of loading everything at once when the application starts.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Simple example

Without lazy loading
App loads
All images, pages, and components load immediately
Slow startup

With lazy loading
---------------------------
App loads
Only visible/required content loads
Other content loads when you scroll or navigate
Faster and smoother

Real-life example 

Think of a restaurant menu:
You don’t cook every dish when the restaurant opens
You cook only what customers order
That’s lazy loading.
-----------------------------------------
Why lazy loading is important

Faster initial page load 
Less memory usage
Better user experience
Saves bandwidth
